.header

.h1 The code

If I want to change anything, I find myself first digging through the source code before I can even
begin to add new functionality. This chapter should help 
finding my way through the code easier.

Djedefre is a Dancer2 fat app.  The app is divided in two parts:

- the Dancer2 erl application
- the javascripts

and the views that glue them together.

.h2 Dancer2 app

Everything is serverd by the Dancer2 app 
.fixed dancr.pl.
The app is somewhat modularized. The main app file contains the routes that
server the HTML pages using the template_toolkit. API calls are served by the
routes in
.fixed api_routes.pm.
All user management is done by
.fixed djedefre_user.pm
including the routes needed for that.
All database access is centralized in
.fixed dje_db.pm.
If someone wants to change the underlying database, only this file (and its equivalent
for the scan scripts) need to be changed. The drawing of a network plot 
is a somewhat complex task. This is separated in the file
.fixed drawing.pm.
Finally, some common functions in
.fixed common_functions.pm
are used in different parts of the app.

.h2 API

Djedefre offers an API to retrieve information or set/change information in 
the database. Accessing the API requires a login:

.pre
curl -L -X POST http://localhost:3000/login \
     -d "username=notandi" \
     -d "pwd=leyndarmal"   \
     -c cookies.txt        \
     -s
.pre

Once logged in, you can retrieve the information:

.pre
curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/api/json/servers \
     -b cookies.txt \
     -H "Accept: application/json"
.pre


